WEBVTT

00:14.146 --> 00:16.106
What kind of an excuse is that?

00:16.189 --> 00:17.357
Huh?

00:17.441 --> 00:20.360
You would've had more chances
when you got to high school.

00:20.444 --> 00:23.739
It's only natural
that there are people better than you.

00:23.822 --> 00:25.365
But that's not the point.

00:25.449 --> 00:27.242
That's not the point at all.

00:31.413 --> 00:32.247
- Well...
- Ah.

00:33.040 --> 00:36.752
It's easy to say the right thing
when you're watching from the sidelines.

00:49.347 --> 00:51.183
Well, sure, but that's what I think!

00:51.266 --> 00:52.893
Ugh, you're just so annoying!

00:52.976 --> 00:55.896
I can't stand
that know-it-all look on your face.

00:57.105 --> 01:00.567
I'm never gonna see Natsu again,
so just let it go!

01:00.650 --> 01:03.320
You came up to her with your bad attitude.

01:03.403 --> 01:04.905
You made things ugly.

01:04.988 --> 01:07.157
That's because someone
who wants to win nationals

01:07.240 --> 01:08.909
shouldn't be fooling around!

01:08.992 --> 01:11.119
She's practicing as much as everyone else!

01:11.203 --> 01:12.996
She used to do more than that!

01:13.080 --> 01:14.790
It was basically all she did!

01:14.873 --> 01:18.376
Chinatsu is good because she trained
more than everyone else.

01:18.460 --> 01:20.921
If she slows down now,
she's not gonna win!

01:25.967 --> 01:27.928
<i>So she's being like this</i>

01:28.512 --> 01:32.099
<i>because deep down,
she's worried about Chinatsu?</i>

01:32.182 --> 01:33.934
- Ms. Goto?
- Huh?

01:34.017 --> 01:36.937
Mr. Inomata? Is something wrong?

01:37.646 --> 01:38.897
No, everything's fine.

01:41.108 --> 01:45.195
<i>One thing's for sure.
Those two can't go on like this.</i>

01:49.491 --> 01:53.703
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

03:16.494 --> 03:20.707
EPISODE 28
THEY'RE ONE AND THE SAME

03:31.927 --> 03:32.969
Morning.

03:36.431 --> 03:39.935
Taiki! Pack those side dishes
in the bento box!

03:40.518 --> 03:41.937
Did you oversleep?

03:42.020 --> 03:44.356
I stayed up way too late
watching K-dramas.

03:45.065 --> 03:46.858
<i>What is she? A teenager?</i>

03:47.943 --> 03:49.361
Where's Chinatsu?

03:50.070 --> 03:54.366
I sent her on ahead.
The Winter Cup is right around the corner.

03:55.659 --> 04:00.038
Make sure she gets that bento box.
Leave it in front of the clubroom.

04:00.121 --> 04:01.122
You got it.

04:03.041 --> 04:05.210
<i>Chinatsu's bento box...</i>

04:06.211 --> 04:07.045
GOOD LUCK

04:07.128 --> 04:10.215
<i>If I wrote a little message,
I wonder if she'd like it.</i>

04:11.841 --> 04:13.218
<i>Like I would do that.</i>

04:14.261 --> 04:16.388
<i>I'll give her the biggest piece of meat.</i>

04:17.013 --> 04:18.640
<i>Lots of vegetables too.</i>

04:18.723 --> 04:20.976
<i>And the best-looking</i> tamagoyaki.

04:23.895 --> 04:26.022
If you do that, the lid won't close.

04:26.106 --> 04:27.399
You think so?

04:29.109 --> 04:30.318
I'm heading out!

04:37.450 --> 04:38.451
Hey, Taiki.

04:39.995 --> 04:41.496
You're late today.

04:41.579 --> 04:43.498
I had to drop by the store.

04:43.581 --> 04:45.166
- Next!
- Okay!

04:46.876 --> 04:48.295
- And next!
- Okay!

04:49.879 --> 04:52.799
So basketball has a tournament coming up?

04:53.883 --> 04:56.052
When one of the clubs
has a tournament game,

04:56.136 --> 04:58.305
the air in the gym changes.

04:58.388 --> 05:00.557
Everything is more tense.

05:01.391 --> 05:03.560
You can feel their nerves
all the way over here.

05:04.144 --> 05:05.061
Yeah.

05:08.815 --> 05:09.858
I feel it too.

05:11.192 --> 05:13.069
- Morning.
- Good morning.

05:15.655 --> 05:17.073
Good morning.

05:21.119 --> 05:22.120
Anyway...

05:22.203 --> 05:23.079
See ya later.

05:26.166 --> 05:27.834
Don't worry about her.

05:28.668 --> 05:30.211
She may act like that,

05:30.295 --> 05:32.839
but her rhythmic gymnastics
have never been better.

05:32.922 --> 05:36.718
It looks like you have way less
of an influence on Hina's life

05:36.801 --> 05:38.053
than we thought, I guess.

05:41.056 --> 05:42.932
<i>What are you trying to say?</i>

06:00.700 --> 06:03.370
Huh? Whose bento is that?

06:03.995 --> 06:05.455
Oh, that's mine.

06:21.012 --> 06:23.139
Chinatsu, we'd better hurry.

06:23.223 --> 06:24.224
Right.

06:27.060 --> 06:27.894
Pass!

06:27.977 --> 06:29.896
Go, go, go!

06:29.979 --> 06:31.898
Let's get that point back!

06:36.361 --> 06:38.363
Nice! Now get back!

06:43.243 --> 06:45.745
- We're back in ten minutes!
- Okay!

06:55.004 --> 06:55.922
- Yuna.
- Huh?

06:56.005 --> 06:56.965
You got a sec?

06:57.966 --> 06:58.967
What is it?

07:00.009 --> 07:01.886
It's about that play earlier.

07:01.970 --> 07:03.888
You could've gone for the shot yourself.

07:04.472 --> 07:06.599
Everyone was focused on guarding Saya.

07:08.059 --> 07:09.978
You don't have to rush into it,

07:10.061 --> 07:12.605
but I think it's okay
if you play more aggressively.

07:12.689 --> 07:16.109
I can go over it with you
either in the mornings or after practice.

07:16.192 --> 07:17.402
Enough!

07:17.485 --> 07:19.154
I'm sorry, okay?

07:19.821 --> 07:21.739
I already know I'm not good enough.

07:21.823 --> 07:23.908
I'm dragging the whole team down.

07:24.492 --> 07:25.910
But Chinatsu,

07:26.578 --> 07:30.665
you have to stop thinking
everyone can work as hard as you do.

07:34.002 --> 07:36.421
Sorry. I'm just stressed out.

07:36.504 --> 07:37.797
It's fine.

07:38.506 --> 07:40.842
It's not like I'm perfect either.

07:40.925 --> 07:42.427
Let's just do our best.

08:09.287 --> 08:11.206
You're here first again?

08:11.289 --> 08:12.499
Huh?

08:12.582 --> 08:15.084
Don't you ever wanna skip practice
to do other stuff?

08:15.877 --> 08:17.003
I can't do that.

08:17.086 --> 08:19.088
I started later than everyone else.

08:19.923 --> 08:22.342
If I don't practice
at least an hour more a day,

08:22.425 --> 08:24.093
I feel like I won't catch up.

08:24.177 --> 08:28.640
An hour a day multiplied by 24 days
is one full day's worth of practice.

08:28.723 --> 08:31.434
A year's worth would be... Let's see here...

08:31.518 --> 08:33.228
It would be, uh...

08:33.311 --> 08:35.355
There's no time to waste on anything else!

08:36.731 --> 08:39.359
Saying it is one thing,
doing it is another.

08:40.026 --> 08:43.196
You pulling that off,
that's your talent, Natsu.

09:10.473 --> 09:12.475
ALARM
STOP - SNOOZE

09:21.025 --> 09:25.405
You have to stop thinking
everyone can work as hard as you do.

09:26.114 --> 09:27.907
Oh, dang it!

09:55.977 --> 09:57.437
Good morning, everybody.

09:57.520 --> 09:58.563
Morning.

09:59.147 --> 10:00.440
Morning, Chinatsu.

10:00.523 --> 10:03.067
I left both your lunches on the table.

10:03.151 --> 10:05.194
They should be packed nicely today.

10:05.778 --> 10:07.196
Didn't oversleep this time?

10:07.280 --> 10:08.698
What do you mean?

10:08.781 --> 10:09.782
You should be grateful

10:09.866 --> 10:13.244
that I wake up this early every morning
to see you two off.

10:13.828 --> 10:15.455
I'm very grateful.

10:15.538 --> 10:16.998
Yes, thank you so much.

10:17.081 --> 10:18.166
Good!

10:18.249 --> 10:20.752
Okay, then who wants a piece of cake?

10:20.835 --> 10:23.004
You get so carried away.

10:29.969 --> 10:31.346
Hey, Taiki...

10:31.429 --> 10:32.263
What's up?

10:32.347 --> 10:33.806
Just curious.

10:33.890 --> 10:36.768
Have you ever thought about
wanting to skip morning practice?

10:38.227 --> 10:39.729
<i>If Chinatsu weren't around,</i>

10:39.812 --> 10:42.607
<i>I think I would've skipped practice
all the time.</i>

10:43.983 --> 10:44.901
Uh...

10:45.610 --> 10:47.695
Yeah, I definitely have.

10:47.779 --> 10:50.198
My first thought is, "I just wanna sleep."

10:51.991 --> 10:53.743
But when that happens,

10:53.826 --> 10:56.204
I try to imagine how I'll feel later.

10:56.788 --> 11:00.041
And if I'm being honest with myself,
I know I'll regret it.

11:00.875 --> 11:04.045
I think of how skipping
is only letting myself down.

11:04.629 --> 11:07.298
That's usually enough
to get me up that day.

11:18.393 --> 11:20.770
Ah, Taiki, you're too earnest.

11:22.480 --> 11:23.856
<i>You're one to talk.</i>

11:45.044 --> 11:46.754
<i>If she's asking about it,</i>

11:47.672 --> 11:51.217
<i>I wonder if Chinatsu
ever feels like taking a break too.</i>

11:52.760 --> 11:54.220
<i>I'm sure she does.</i>

11:54.303 --> 11:57.974
<i>Her nonstop routine started
because Yumeka was around.</i>

11:58.683 --> 12:01.310
<i>But she still doesn't take a break.</i>

12:01.394 --> 12:02.979
<i>That's just like her.</i>

12:07.692 --> 12:09.986
<i>Yumeka has the wrong idea.</i>

12:11.070 --> 12:14.615
<i>It's true that Chinatsu is continuing
to work hard on her own,</i>

12:15.700 --> 12:17.994
<i>but that's only because she has a goal.</i>

12:19.287 --> 12:21.622
<i>Still, she must be tired.</i>

12:22.623 --> 12:27.420
<i>I really wish that
Yumeka had stayed by Chinatsu's side.</i>

12:30.381 --> 12:32.133
Where's the girls' basketball team?

12:32.216 --> 12:34.510
I heard they have a practice game
in the morning.

12:35.762 --> 12:37.054
- Excuse me.
- Oh.

12:37.138 --> 12:39.265
Oh, look. How's it going there, Coach?

12:39.348 --> 12:42.560
I've got a ticket to the girls'
first Winter Cup game.

12:42.643 --> 12:43.895
Anyone want it?

12:43.978 --> 12:46.022
Eh, my wife bought it,

12:46.105 --> 12:49.400
but she's going back to her parents' house
because her mother hurt her back,

12:49.484 --> 12:51.277
so I've got an extra one.

12:51.360 --> 12:53.404
It's a good seat,
right next to the basket.

12:53.488 --> 12:55.907
Me, me, me, me! I want it, sir!

12:56.866 --> 12:57.909
Sure, kid, it's yours.

12:57.992 --> 13:00.411
- Let's go.
- But don't you have practice that day?

13:00.495 --> 13:02.747
Huh? Uh... I, uh...

13:02.830 --> 13:04.665
It's for a friend, actually.

13:05.792 --> 13:08.294
In that case, I'll take the ticket.

13:09.128 --> 13:10.713
Ahh!

13:10.797 --> 13:13.424
It should go to someone
who's gonna watch, right?

13:13.508 --> 13:15.051
I don't care either way.

13:15.134 --> 13:16.677
No way! You can't have it!

13:16.761 --> 13:17.762
Why not?

13:17.845 --> 13:21.432
It's more important for me to watch anyway
since I'm in basketball club.

13:21.516 --> 13:23.559
I was the one who asked for it first!

13:23.643 --> 13:26.062
He never said
it was first come, first serve.

13:26.938 --> 13:30.608
<i>The last thing I want
is this guy getting close to Chinatsu!</i>

13:31.400 --> 13:34.195
Well, there's a saying,
"He who strikes first wins."

13:34.278 --> 13:37.990
Wow, haven't heard a Japanese expression
like that in forever.

13:38.074 --> 13:40.743
<i>He plays the exchange student card
whenever he wants!</i>

13:40.827 --> 13:43.746
Hmm. Good luck sorting it all out.

13:43.830 --> 13:46.624
In that case,
why don't we compete to decide?

13:46.707 --> 13:50.127
Let's see here. How about if...

13:50.211 --> 13:53.381
Whoever can last longest
in a shuttle run wins.

13:54.715 --> 13:56.008
A shuttle run?

13:56.092 --> 13:58.636
There'd be a gap
if we played each other's sports, right?

13:58.719 --> 14:00.638
Running would be a lot more fair.

14:00.721 --> 14:03.057
After all,
it's just jogging back and forth.

14:04.851 --> 14:06.269
Is that fair?

14:06.352 --> 14:09.313
Wouldn't a basketball player
have an advantage in endurance?

14:09.397 --> 14:11.524
Plus, Matsuoka's a year older.

14:11.607 --> 14:15.403
He said he ran ten kilometers a day
when he was in America.

14:15.486 --> 14:18.656
No matter how you look at it,
Matsuoka's the favorite.

14:19.407 --> 14:20.491
What do you say?

14:22.076 --> 14:23.202
You're on.

14:24.787 --> 14:27.415
<i>You will hear a five-second countdown.</i>

14:27.498 --> 14:29.959
<i>After that, the test will begin.</i>

14:31.669 --> 14:32.920
<i>Five seconds to start.</i>

14:33.504 --> 14:36.257
<i>Three, two, one.</i>

14:37.008 --> 14:37.842
<i>Begin.</i>

14:52.064 --> 14:55.026
Are we really going back
to school for more practice?

14:55.109 --> 14:57.320
We already gave it our all
during the scrimmage.

14:57.904 --> 14:59.989
This way, we can review right away.

15:00.072 --> 15:02.992
Couldn't they have at least gotten us
a bus back or something?

15:03.075 --> 15:05.328
It's not a long way, you know.

15:08.414 --> 15:10.333
I'm going to my house
for a change of clothes,

15:10.416 --> 15:12.084
and then I'll meet you guys over there.

15:12.168 --> 15:13.336
Mmm-hmm. Copy that.

15:23.429 --> 15:28.351
KIKUCHI DENTAL CLINIC

15:28.434 --> 15:31.604
<i>This is the dentist that Taiki goes to.</i>

15:31.687 --> 15:34.357
Look. You're better off not going there.

15:34.982 --> 15:37.068
Thanks for running our errands.

15:37.151 --> 15:39.070
I'll be back in 30 minutes.

15:41.113 --> 15:42.740
I'll see you later...

15:48.871 --> 15:50.289
Oh, Ms. Goto?

15:50.373 --> 15:53.459
Could you also pick up some toilet paper
while you're out?

15:53.542 --> 15:54.418
Sure.

15:58.089 --> 15:59.131
Goto?

16:01.717 --> 16:04.136
I thought that your last name was Kido.

16:04.971 --> 16:07.723
My parents got divorced
when I graduated middle school,

16:07.807 --> 16:09.392
so my last name changed.

16:10.601 --> 16:11.936
I had no idea.

16:12.979 --> 16:15.272
It's not exactly uncommon.

16:15.356 --> 16:16.857
I didn't think to mention...

16:19.026 --> 16:22.947
Wow, Yumeka.
You really don't tell me anything.

16:34.417 --> 16:36.877
Do they want that ticket that badly?

16:37.670 --> 16:39.547
Is it really worth all this running?

16:39.630 --> 16:40.464
Hmm.

16:41.215 --> 16:43.634
There must be something more to it.

16:43.718 --> 16:44.802
What do you mean?

16:44.885 --> 16:47.805
Your steps are getting sluggish,
aren't they, fanboy?

16:47.888 --> 16:49.807
Don't know what you're talking about!

16:51.809 --> 16:53.185
Glad to hear it.

16:53.269 --> 16:55.730
Because I'm not even
feeling warmed up yet.

16:56.439 --> 16:58.482
<i>He's totally unfazed.</i>

17:00.568 --> 17:02.987
Hey, and while we're at it,

17:03.070 --> 17:04.989
why don't we say that the loser...

17:05.573 --> 17:08.743
agrees to give up on pursuing Natsu, hmm?

17:10.661 --> 17:12.997
There's no way I'd agree to that.

17:14.498 --> 17:17.334
I'm not giving up my feelings
over something this dumb!

17:17.418 --> 17:18.878
Huh. I see.

17:20.004 --> 17:20.838
But still...

17:24.341 --> 17:27.762
I think we can agree
that if you end up losing to me,

17:27.845 --> 17:29.805
it's gonna look super lame.

17:37.271 --> 17:39.398
You don't tell me anything, huh?

17:46.405 --> 17:48.282
Do you work here part-time?

17:50.367 --> 17:51.410
I do.

17:52.953 --> 17:54.622
<i>Then Taiki knew too...</i>

17:59.001 --> 18:01.128
Did you move to another school

18:01.212 --> 18:03.172
because of what happened
with your parents?

18:04.048 --> 18:06.300
It's got nothing to do with that.

18:06.383 --> 18:07.676
I see.

18:08.677 --> 18:12.056
That's the kind of thing
I wish you'd told me.

18:13.474 --> 18:15.017
I know just because I'm your friend,

18:15.101 --> 18:18.145
that doesn't mean
you have to tell me everything.

18:18.229 --> 18:20.231
Because I don't know how you feel.

18:22.316 --> 18:24.193
It is your life. I can't change that.

18:24.902 --> 18:26.237
I can't change that.

18:33.869 --> 18:36.080
Sorry. I'll let you shop now.

18:39.542 --> 18:41.544
How was I supposed to tell you?!

18:43.754 --> 18:45.923
You don't wanna see my weak side.

18:46.757 --> 18:47.925
<i>Do you, Natsu?</i>

18:52.263 --> 18:54.932
'Cause then I wouldn't be
your role model anymore.

18:59.937 --> 19:01.522
And sure,

19:01.605 --> 19:04.942
we had a lot of fun times
back when we were friends.

19:05.526 --> 19:08.696
<i>I was always that teammate
who could teach you about basketball.</i>

19:08.779 --> 19:10.948
<i>You depended on me.</i>

19:11.031 --> 19:12.950
<i>At first, that made me happy.</i>

19:14.034 --> 19:15.744
But then, somehow,

19:16.787 --> 19:19.206
I started to lose
my passion for basketball.

19:21.542 --> 19:22.877
You're lying.

19:22.960 --> 19:24.378
I'm not lying.

19:28.757 --> 19:31.969
So listen, me and your dad...

19:33.012 --> 19:36.473
Deep down, I'm not as cool
as you think I am, Chinatsu.

19:37.474 --> 19:39.894
<i>I often thought about skipping practice.</i>

19:39.977 --> 19:43.189
<i>And when I realized
that having talent didn't matter,</i>

19:43.981 --> 19:45.900
<i>I wanted to be done altogether.</i>

19:47.234 --> 19:49.361
Because the truth is,

19:49.445 --> 19:51.447
I was the one looking up to you.

19:53.699 --> 19:55.910
You never wanted to skip practice.

19:56.535 --> 20:00.664
You just quietly did what you had to do,
and that made you amazing.

20:00.748 --> 20:03.667
I was embarrassed
by how different I was from you,

20:04.251 --> 20:06.170
<i>and I started to hate myself.</i>

20:07.880 --> 20:10.174
How could I tell you something like that?

20:13.802 --> 20:18.015
But her ability to work hard,
I do admire that.

20:19.141 --> 20:22.686
You pulling that off,
that's your talent, Natsu.

20:25.773 --> 20:28.442
One time, I happened to notice you.

20:29.151 --> 20:31.946
<i>It was the day after our last game
in middle school...</i>

20:37.159 --> 20:39.662
<i>and you were practicing all by yourself.</i>

20:41.413 --> 20:43.958
I was in a slump after we lost,

20:44.041 --> 20:47.169
only feeling a sense of relief
that it was all over.

20:47.836 --> 20:48.921
But you...

20:51.048 --> 20:54.051
I imagined
it must have been really frustrating,

20:54.134 --> 20:58.264
seeing that you worked so hard
and only to end up disappointed.

21:02.184 --> 21:04.853
That's why I was so shocked
when I saw you.

21:05.729 --> 21:07.690
<i>Hanging out with some guy.</i>

21:08.983 --> 21:13.195
<i>That's not the same determined Natsu
who made me feel like giving up.</i>

21:13.696 --> 21:17.116
She loves basketball!
She doesn't care about anything else!

21:17.783 --> 21:19.994
<i>All she does is practice!</i>

21:20.077 --> 21:21.745
'Cause that's who she is!

21:21.829 --> 21:23.122
You're wrong.

21:25.207 --> 21:26.875
He's not just some guy.

21:28.961 --> 21:31.380
<i>It all comes down to one thing.</i>

21:34.675 --> 21:36.385
When you quit basketball,

21:37.094 --> 21:38.387
<i>I lost my best friend</i>

21:39.555 --> 21:42.391
<i>and the one person I could always rely on.</i>

21:43.934 --> 21:45.352
I was so lonely.

21:48.939 --> 21:51.900
<i>Winning nationals was such a far-off goal</i>

21:53.152 --> 21:55.863
<i>that when I started to doubt</i>

21:55.946 --> 21:59.491
<i>if all this constant practicing
was really worth it or not...</i>

22:04.997 --> 22:06.915
<i>or when I felt like giving up...</i>

22:09.084 --> 22:10.919
<i>I had a source of strength.</i>

22:15.591 --> 22:17.509
<i>It's because I have someone like him</i>

22:18.510 --> 22:20.304
that I'm able to do my best!
